oncall-alice: PagerDuty triggered for high 5xx rate from hosted API in us-west-2. Alert shows sustained error ratio ~14% for the last 6m. Paging now.

pagerduty-bot: Incident #INC-2026-025 opened by monitoring. Escalation: eng-oncall paging policy level 2.

mia-sre: I'm hopping in. Seeing spike correlating with a surge from a small set of API keys — 3 clients account for ~82% of offending requests.

sam-platform: Thanks. Can we put an emergency soft quota on those keys and enable a 429 fast-fail path for streaming endpoints?

oncall-alice: Yes. I'm going to apply a temporary rate cap per-key (100 rps -> 20 rps) and enable short-lived quota overrides. Doing now: `rb admin quotas set --key client-A --rps 20 --reason "live mitigation"`

eng-sdks: Heads-up — SDK clients might retry aggressively on 429s. We should coordinate guidance for backoff so we don't trigger retry storms.

paul-cs: I'm already triaging customer impact. Client-A is a partner; raising to them now. Need clear messaging for customers who see 429s and partial streaming disconnects.

mia-sre: Applied caps to client-A/B/C. Metrics show error ratio dropping toward baseline. But we still see tail latencies for streaming requests. I'm going to disable server-side streaming for those keys as a fallback (switch to chunked polling).

oncall-alice: Command executed: `rb admin feature-toggle disable --feature streaming --scope key:client-A,client-B,client-C --ttl 00:30`

eng-sdks: Important: If streaming is disabled server-side, older SDKs will immediately try to reconnect. Recommend guidance: exponential backoff with jitter and idempotency keys for any non-idempotent operations. Example snippet to share with customers:

```
// recommended retry wrapper (pseudo-js)
async function retry(fn, attempts=5){
  for(let i=0;i<attempts;i++){
    try { return await fn(); } catch(e){
      if(e.status===429 || e.status===503){
        const base = Math.min(1000 * Math.pow(2,i), 16000);
        await sleep(base * (0.5 + Math.random()/2)); // full jitter
      } else throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

And note: include an `idempotency_key` header for operations that might be retried.

sam-platform: Also add guidance to reduce concurrency per-connection for SDKs (max inflight tokens=8) and to respect `Retry-After` header when present. We'll push a short doc to docs.redwood.dev/mitigations.

paul-cs: Messaging sent to affected customers: "We have temporarily applied per-key rate caps and disabled streaming to maintain platform stability. Please implement exponential backoff with jitter and idempotency keys. We'll notify when caps are lifted." :email:

mia-sre: Observability check: created a dashboard panel showing per-key 5xx, per-key rps, retry rates, and `Retry-After` adherence. Patch: `dashId=mit-185124`.

oncall-alice: On-call handoff in 25m to sam-platform. Current mitigation timeline: caps + streaming toggle + customer guidance in place. Next steps: monitor for 30m, if stable start rolling caps to 50 rps and re-enable streaming in controlled canary for one key.

eng-sdks: Quick note for SDKs: add an opt-in compatibility mode that auto-detects server streaming disabled via `X-Streaming-Disabled: true` response header and falls back to polling. Example header check in client: `if(resp.headers['x-streaming-disabled']) switchToPolling()`

mia-sre: Telemetry: 10m after caps, total 5xx count down 78%. Retry traffic increased ~12% but most retries respect Retry-After.

sam-platform: I'll take the handoff. Oncall next window: sam-platform -> monitor 1851241800-1851245400. If metrics continue improving, plan to incrementally relax caps in 10m steps.

oncall-alice: Leaving notes in the incident runbook: mitigation steps, commands used, affected keys list, customer outreach copy. If anyone automates this flow later, we should include a safe-guarded circuit-breaker to avoid cascading retries.

paul-cs: Customer follow-up: request to whitelist limited bursts for partner B during afternoon maintenance window — deferring approval until metrics fully recovered.

eng-sdks: Will publish an example retry/backoff patch and a short migration note by EOD. Also adding an idempotency helper utility to SDKs (Header: `Idempotency-Key`).

pagerduty-bot: Incident #INC-2026-025: status changed to "monitoring".

oncall-alice: Closing thread here; will update incident timeline and attach logs. If anyone sees regressions, ping me directly. :thumbsup:
